WEBVTT

00:00:00.840 --> 00:00:03.840
It is indeed the time to start Kaleido Star.

00:00:03.840 --> 00:00:05.510
When you watch Kaleido Star,

00:00:05.510 --> 00:00:06.780
I think you should keep your room brightly lit

00:00:06.780 --> 00:00:09.610
and sit as far from the TV as you can.

00:00:11.750 --> 00:00:12.950
Well, well, well.

00:00:12.950 --> 00:00:16.080
Have you ever had something
important to you end?

00:00:16.320 --> 00:00:18.320
When we had fun, when we had tough times,

00:00:18.320 --> 00:00:19.760
when we laughed and cried,

00:00:19.760 --> 00:00:21.960
the precious memories
that we spent together.

00:00:21.960 --> 00:00:24.480
Being thankful for many, many things.

00:00:24.630 --> 00:00:27.160
But, we can't let it end like this.
Don't you think?

00:00:27.160 --> 00:00:28.460
Don't you think? Don't you think?

00:00:30.670 --> 00:00:35.670
<i>The dream everyone is looking for
must be someplace</i>

00:00:30.670 --> 00:00:35.670
<i>Dare mo sagashiteru yume wa kitto aru</i>

00:00:35.670 --> 00:00:38.170
<i>It has to be somewhere</i>

00:00:35.670 --> 00:00:38.170
<i>Dokoka ni aru</i>

00:00:38.170 --> 00:00:45.880
<i>Until your dream comes true someday,
you're not alone</i>

00:00:38.170 --> 00:00:45.880
<i>Negai ga itsuka kanau made hitori ja nai</i>

00:00:53.920 --> 00:01:00.230
<i>Remember how I used to say
I could make it to the end?</i>

00:00:53.920 --> 00:01:00.230
<i>Saigo made yareru to ittetane</i>

00:01:00.230 --> 00:01:06.600
<i>I must have been pretending to be tough</i>

00:01:00.230 --> 00:01:06.600
<i>Kitto tsuyogatte itanda</i>

00:01:06.600 --> 00:01:15.310
<i>Everything I did was reckless
and it never got me anywhere</i>

00:01:06.600 --> 00:01:15.310
<i>Itsudatte muchabakka de
zutto karamawari de</i>

00:01:15.310 --> 00:01:21.840
<i>But you alone were always beside me</i>

00:01:15.310 --> 00:01:21.840
<i>Dakedo anata dake ga soba ni ita</i>

00:01:23.650 --> 00:01:28.560
<i>The dream everyone is looking for
must be somewhere</i>

00:01:23.650 --> 00:01:28.560
<i>Daremo sagashiteru yume wa kitto aru</i>

00:01:28.560 --> 00:01:31.160
<i>You can start going forward</i>

00:01:28.560 --> 00:01:31.160
<i>Aruki daseru</i>

00:01:31.160 --> 00:01:36.700
<i>From this moment, something will start</i>

00:01:31.160 --> 00:01:36.700
<i>Koko kara nani kaga hajimaru</i>

00:01:36.700 --> 00:01:38.730
<i>I want to believe that</i>

00:01:36.700 --> 00:01:38.730
<i>Shinjite itai</i>

00:01:38.730 --> 00:01:46.240
<i>The light I haven't seen yet
is beaming toward the promised place</i>

00:01:38.730 --> 00:01:46.240
<i>Mada minu hikari yakusoku no
basho e to tsuzuite yuku</i>

00:01:46.240 --> 00:01:56.710
<i>Until your dream comes true someday,
you're not alone</i>

00:01:46.240 --> 00:01:56.710
<i>Negai ga itsuka kanau made hitori ja naisa</i>

00:02:07.900 --> 00:02:09.890
Sora! It was the best!

00:02:10.330 --> 00:02:12.200
Two weeks from the opening day,

00:02:12.200 --> 00:02:14.300
the audience's reaction started changing.

00:02:14.300 --> 00:02:15.670
Did you read today's newspaper?

00:02:15.670 --> 00:02:18.070
Of course I did.

00:02:19.410 --> 00:02:22.840
Kaleido Stage's new director, Mia Guillem.

00:02:22.840 --> 00:02:26.010
Her appearance has been more dramatic
than Halley's Comet!

00:02:26.820 --> 00:02:28.720
Well, of course,
I deserve to get that comment.

00:02:37.690 --> 00:02:39.630
Don't think you'll get away with this!

00:02:41.700 --> 00:02:42.100
Yuri's Amazing Trap

00:02:42.100 --> 00:02:44.730
Yuri's Amazing Trap

00:02:42.100 --> 00:02:44.730
"Yuri's Amazing Trap"

00:02:44.730 --> 00:02:47.630
Yuri's Amazing Trap

00:02:49.370 --> 00:02:52.470
There was concern that Kaleido Stage
would grow smaller and weaker.

00:02:52.470 --> 00:02:55.970
However, there is plenty of possibility
that it will regain its strength.

00:02:56.040 --> 00:02:58.110
It really could be.

00:02:58.110 --> 00:03:00.150
It means that no matter how
Yuri tries to obstruct us,

00:03:00.150 --> 00:03:02.950
people cannot ignore a real nice show.

00:03:03.220 --> 00:03:05.990
I've seen all kinds of shows,

00:03:05.990 --> 00:03:08.890
but, even setting aside favoritism,
I think this show is wonderful.

00:03:09.090 --> 00:03:10.060
What?

00:03:10.060 --> 00:03:11.760
Are you serious?

00:03:11.760 --> 00:03:13.800
My dad is an old-fashioned type kind of man.

00:03:13.800 --> 00:03:15.230
So, he cannot tell a lie.

00:03:16.130 --> 00:03:17.560
Hey, Marion...

00:03:19.370 --> 00:03:23.030
Oh, it would be nice if this show keeps
on like this and becomes a long-run.

00:03:23.240 --> 00:03:25.210
No way.

00:03:25.210 --> 00:03:28.180
But, if the audience keeps growing like this...

00:03:28.540 --> 00:03:30.570
Maybe we'll even get
lots of sponsors signing on.

00:03:34.920 --> 00:03:37.010
I don't think you should get
overexcited about this.

00:03:37.820 --> 00:03:40.360
Anna, you missed the timing
at the very beginning.

00:03:40.360 --> 00:03:42.480
Mia, your face is too tense sometimes.

00:03:42.890 --> 00:03:45.760
Sora, you let yourself go,
and make your moves too fast.

00:03:45.760 --> 00:03:48.260
If you keep doing that, the lighting
technician cannot keep up with you.

00:03:48.260 --> 00:03:49.990
You cannot call our performance perfect
by any means.

00:03:50.300 --> 00:03:51.090
Oh...

00:03:51.230 --> 00:03:52.470
Oh...

00:03:52.470 --> 00:03:53.400
But...

00:03:54.500 --> 00:03:57.130
This show is not too bad.

00:03:59.210 --> 00:04:01.340
Just now, was that...

00:04:01.340 --> 00:04:02.540
Praise?

00:04:02.780 --> 00:04:04.070
Did she praise... us?

00:04:04.280 --> 00:04:07.010
I can tell by the way she talks.
She likes the show a lot.

00:04:08.080 --> 00:04:10.190
Miss Layla is praising us!

00:04:10.190 --> 00:04:12.090
That makes me happier than
any other good critiques.

00:04:12.490 --> 00:04:14.460
Aim for a long-run! Yeah! Yeah!

00:04:14.790 --> 00:04:16.020
In order to make that happen,

00:04:16.020 --> 00:04:18.890
we should brace ourselves for the
remainder of the two weeks and perform.

00:04:19.230 --> 00:04:20.060
Yes.

00:04:21.460 --> 00:04:23.990
Now, I'm getting motivated! Yeah!

00:04:24.200 --> 00:04:26.100
Me, too. Yeah!

00:04:26.300 --> 00:04:26.700
Yeah!

00:04:26.700 --> 00:04:27.500
Yeah!

00:04:26.700 --> 00:04:27.500
Yeah!

00:04:27.640 --> 00:04:28.140
Yeah!

00:04:28.140 --> 00:04:28.570
Yeah!

00:04:28.140 --> 00:04:28.570
Yeah!

00:04:28.570 --> 00:04:28.970
Yeah!

00:04:28.570 --> 00:04:28.970
Yeah!

00:04:28.570 --> 00:04:28.970
Yeah!

00:04:29.200 --> 00:04:30.000
Yeah!

00:04:30.470 --> 00:04:33.480
For the sake of Kaleido Stage's future!

00:04:33.480 --> 00:04:34.440
Yeah!

00:04:47.460 --> 00:04:48.620
Death...

00:04:48.620 --> 00:04:51.180
The ending of things.

00:04:51.360 --> 00:04:54.520
Excuse me, please stop with the
inauspicious fortune-telling.

00:04:54.660 --> 00:04:57.730
Kaleido Stage is at the critical moment
whether it can survive or perish.

00:04:57.730 --> 00:04:59.770
So can you produce brighter futures?

00:04:59.770 --> 00:05:02.260
Well, there is no meaning in fortune-telling.

00:05:03.140 --> 00:05:04.370
Sora! It's happening!

00:05:04.970 --> 00:05:06.140
Ugh... swallowed it.

00:05:06.140 --> 00:05:07.640
It's not the time for
saying something like that.

00:05:07.640 --> 00:05:09.370
People are filled with a practice room!

00:05:09.980 --> 00:05:10.910
You just said something funny!

00:05:10.910 --> 00:05:11.080
Why now? I didn't intend it to be funny!

00:05:10.910 --> 00:05:11.080
You just said something funny!

00:05:11.080 --> 00:05:11.880
Why now? I didn't intend it to be funny!

00:05:11.880 --> 00:05:12.250
Why now? I didn't intend it to be funny!

00:05:11.880 --> 00:05:12.250
Anyway, please come!

00:05:12.250 --> 00:05:13.510
Anyway, please come!

00:05:17.720 --> 00:05:18.980
What's going on?

00:05:19.320 --> 00:05:20.980
I thought everyone quit.

00:05:21.260 --> 00:05:22.690
I'm not dreaming, right?

00:05:23.020 --> 00:05:25.190
Maybe everyone decided to come back

00:05:25.190 --> 00:05:27.560
after they heard about
Kaleido Stage's reputation.

00:05:27.560 --> 00:05:29.560
As I expected... It's happening?

00:05:29.560 --> 00:05:32.000
After all, this is the show that
Miss Layla praised.

00:05:32.000 --> 00:05:35.770
Seriously, the revival of Kaleido Stage
may not be a dream.

00:05:35.770 --> 00:05:39.510
I guess you need to rewrite "Freedom"
with more people, Mia.

00:05:39.510 --> 00:05:40.870
Let me handle it.

00:05:41.780 --> 00:05:43.210
Oh, I didn't know you were here.

00:05:43.910 --> 00:05:44.810
Ken.

00:05:44.980 --> 00:05:47.570
Everyone, Boss wants us to gather
in his room right away.

00:05:47.750 --> 00:05:48.810
What?

00:05:48.880 --> 00:05:51.350
I wonder if it means... As we thought...

00:05:51.350 --> 00:05:51.720
Yeah!

00:05:51.720 --> 00:05:52.850
The announcement of his decision
to make this a long-run?

00:05:51.720 --> 00:05:52.850
Yeah!

00:05:52.850 --> 00:05:54.790
The announcement of his decision
to make this a long-run?

00:06:10.570 --> 00:06:11.570
Come in.

00:06:11.570 --> 00:06:12.910
Ready?

00:06:12.910 --> 00:06:15.070
Congratulations!

00:06:15.740 --> 00:06:17.300
Eh?

00:06:21.850 --> 00:06:22.650
Hello...

00:06:22.750 --> 00:06:24.190
Yuri...

00:06:24.190 --> 00:06:25.450
Why you are here?

00:06:25.720 --> 00:06:28.450
Kalos, why don't you explain it to them?

00:06:32.530 --> 00:06:34.160
Then, I have no choice.

00:06:34.160 --> 00:06:36.530
I will explain the situation to them.

00:06:36.530 --> 00:06:38.630
Well, it's simple.

00:06:38.630 --> 00:06:41.930
Kalos will no longer be the
owner of Kaleido Stage after today.

00:06:43.740 --> 00:06:46.570
Instead, I will be the owner.

00:06:47.080 --> 00:06:50.670
The current Kaleido Stage will be
dissolved after today's show.

00:06:50.910 --> 00:06:52.000
What!

00:06:52.510 --> 00:06:55.280
Kaleido Stage will be dissolved?

00:06:55.980 --> 00:06:57.140
It can't be...

00:06:57.320 --> 00:06:58.810
It's true.

00:06:59.090 --> 00:07:02.590
But, we still have two weeks to perform.

00:07:02.590 --> 00:07:04.660
The audience is packed.

00:07:04.660 --> 00:07:06.390
There is no reason to quit.

00:07:06.560 --> 00:07:07.460
She's right.

00:07:07.460 --> 00:07:10.900
If the show keeps on like this,
even a long-run is a possibility.

00:07:14.170 --> 00:07:19.200
Kalos, don't tell me you were also
dreaming a foolish dream like them. Right?

00:07:20.040 --> 00:07:21.540
A long-run?

00:07:21.540 --> 00:07:23.840
An amateur show like this?

00:07:24.510 --> 00:07:25.410
It will never happen.

00:07:26.380 --> 00:07:27.640
Hey, apologize to everyone!

00:07:29.820 --> 00:07:30.250
Get your hands off me!

00:07:30.250 --> 00:07:31.220
As for the rest of tickets for after today,
we will refund them.

00:07:30.250 --> 00:07:31.220
Get your hands off me!

00:07:31.220 --> 00:07:32.690
As for the rest of tickets for after today,
we will refund them.

00:07:31.220 --> 00:07:32.690
Oof!

00:07:32.690 --> 00:07:33.620
As for the rest of tickets for after today,
we will refund them.

00:07:33.890 --> 00:07:34.880
Ouch!

00:07:35.160 --> 00:07:36.860
Leave Anna alone!

00:07:36.860 --> 00:07:37.760
Let her go!

00:07:37.760 --> 00:07:38.990
Damn!

00:07:38.990 --> 00:07:39.980
Let her go.

00:07:40.760 --> 00:07:41.660
Anna...

00:07:41.660 --> 00:07:43.160
Are you all right, Anna?

00:07:43.160 --> 00:07:47.260
Both Kenneth Corporation and Hamilton
Foundation backed out as investors.

00:07:47.800 --> 00:07:50.170
Your Kaleido Stage is over.

00:07:50.170 --> 00:07:51.200
It will not exist.

00:07:51.770 --> 00:07:56.240
Layla, by Mr. Hamilton's request,
I can't make a contract with you.

00:07:56.240 --> 00:07:59.440
But, if you wish,
I don't mind persuading him.

00:07:59.810 --> 00:08:03.550
Of course, I know all of your talents.

00:08:03.550 --> 00:08:05.880
I definitely want you to join
my Kaleido Stage.

00:08:06.350 --> 00:08:07.590
I'll welcome all of you.

00:08:07.590 --> 00:08:08.720
No thank you.

00:08:08.720 --> 00:08:09.960
Me neither.

00:08:09.960 --> 00:08:11.720
I also decline.

00:08:12.030 --> 00:08:14.000
Really? That's too bad.

00:08:14.000 --> 00:08:18.060
Then, consequently, I must also ask you
to get out of the dormitory.

00:08:21.270 --> 00:08:22.600
My speech is finished.

00:08:37.020 --> 00:08:39.820
Yes, I sold all rights.

00:08:39.820 --> 00:08:41.580
So you should quit, too.

00:08:41.920 --> 00:08:43.290
Why?

00:08:43.730 --> 00:08:46.660
There is a time for everything.

00:08:46.660 --> 00:08:50.000
The current Kaleido Stage
is practically a corpse.

00:08:50.000 --> 00:08:53.570
Just thinking that you're still there
makes my blood run cold.

00:08:53.570 --> 00:08:57.060
Father, Kaleido Stage is not dead yet.

00:08:57.270 --> 00:09:00.740
Layla, you did more than enough.

00:09:00.740 --> 00:09:04.080
I will set up the management office
for you shortly.

00:09:04.080 --> 00:09:05.780
There are many fields where you can
make the most of your talents

00:09:05.780 --> 00:09:07.870
in either in the movies or on the stage.

00:09:07.980 --> 00:09:09.650
You can do whatever you want.

00:09:09.650 --> 00:09:11.920
First, appear on the screen again.

00:09:11.920 --> 00:09:16.820
I heard your last movie got good reviews.
I think doing movies suits you.

00:09:16.890 --> 00:09:24.060
I don't think you understand how much
Kaleido Stage means to me now.

00:09:25.270 --> 00:09:26.830
If you say it's that much,

00:09:26.830 --> 00:09:30.370
do you want to participate in
Yuri's Kaleido Stage for a while?

00:09:30.370 --> 00:09:32.200
That would be meaningless.

00:09:32.740 --> 00:09:35.940
Layla, then what do you want to do?

00:09:36.280 --> 00:09:39.410
Well, I wonder what I want to do.

00:09:40.150 --> 00:09:43.640
Maybe, I don't want to lose...

00:09:43.750 --> 00:09:46.410
I don't want to lose the partner
who motivates me so much...

00:09:47.820 --> 00:09:48.980
Partner...

00:09:49.260 --> 00:09:52.450
If you start doing something new,
you will forget about it soon enough.

00:09:52.760 --> 00:09:54.460
I doubt it.

00:09:54.460 --> 00:09:58.570
In any case, the current Kaleido Stage
will not exist after tonight's show.

00:09:58.570 --> 00:10:00.430
That is something I cannot change.

00:10:00.700 --> 00:10:02.100
I understand.

00:10:02.740 --> 00:10:05.140
Layla... When you look back later,

00:10:05.140 --> 00:10:08.910
you will think you're glad
that you did what I told you to do.

00:10:09.080 --> 00:10:10.040
Yes.

00:10:18.820 --> 00:10:20.690
So, this evening is the last.

00:10:20.690 --> 00:10:22.420
I can't believe it.

00:10:22.420 --> 00:10:24.690
Anyway, let's put everything into it.

00:10:27.130 --> 00:10:29.960
But I'm afraid I'll start crying
while I'm on stage.

00:10:30.260 --> 00:10:31.700
You can't help it.

00:10:31.700 --> 00:10:33.100
Because this will be the last.

00:10:45.250 --> 00:10:46.110
STOP CRYING!

00:10:47.980 --> 00:10:49.180
Everyone,

00:10:49.180 --> 00:10:52.210
do you think it's okay to appear
in the last show feeling like you do now?

00:10:53.720 --> 00:10:55.120
Even if you keep crying,

00:10:55.120 --> 00:10:58.150
nothing will change the fact that
today is the last show.

00:10:59.360 --> 00:11:00.520
Yes.

00:11:01.930 --> 00:11:04.560
We should not appear on the stage
like the way we feel right now.

00:11:05.000 --> 00:11:06.430
You're right, Ken.

00:11:06.430 --> 00:11:08.600
Since this is the last performance,

00:11:08.600 --> 00:11:13.340
I want show the audience the
best performance more than ever.

00:11:13.510 --> 00:11:14.510
Right?

00:11:14.510 --> 00:11:19.310
In order to let the audience keep the memory
of our Kaleido Stage in their hearts forever!

00:11:19.680 --> 00:11:20.480
Yes.

00:11:20.580 --> 00:11:21.410
Yes.

00:11:21.680 --> 00:11:22.880
That's right.

00:11:22.880 --> 00:11:23.980
We have to do our best so we don't regret.

00:11:24.520 --> 00:11:26.320
It's not the time to be depressed.

00:11:26.690 --> 00:11:28.060
Thank you, Ken.

00:11:28.060 --> 00:11:29.660
Somehow, you brought me to my senses.

00:11:29.660 --> 00:11:31.120
That's more like you, Sora.

00:11:31.590 --> 00:11:33.360
Boss must feel the same way.

00:11:33.630 --> 00:11:36.460
I don't know what happened in the past,

00:11:36.460 --> 00:11:40.400
but the Kaleido Stage that he built up
with care will be gone.

00:11:40.840 --> 00:11:44.770
I'll go to see the Boss
and tell him how we all feel.

00:11:54.050 --> 00:11:55.120
It's Sora.

00:11:55.120 --> 00:11:56.210
Come in.

00:11:56.880 --> 00:11:58.220
Excuse me.

00:12:02.090 --> 00:12:05.190
Just a moment ago, we all talked backstage.

00:12:05.190 --> 00:12:07.630
Everyone feels the same way.

00:12:07.630 --> 00:12:09.900
Although today is our last show...

00:12:09.900 --> 00:12:12.700
No... Because it's the last show,

00:12:12.700 --> 00:12:14.670
Let's make it the best show.

00:12:14.940 --> 00:12:18.630
Boss, do you have anything
you want me to tell everybody?

00:12:19.610 --> 00:12:22.080
There is one thing I want to say.

00:12:22.080 --> 00:12:24.350
If you're going to prepare yourself
for the stage like that,

00:12:24.350 --> 00:12:25.840
it's better not to do it.

00:12:26.110 --> 00:12:27.840
What?

00:12:28.180 --> 00:12:31.640
What do you mean by that?

00:12:33.520 --> 00:12:34.890
Since it is the last,

00:12:34.890 --> 00:12:36.950
we want to do our best
and make it the best show.

00:12:37.190 --> 00:12:40.320
Are you saying that is wrong?

00:12:40.460 --> 00:12:46.560
Wanting to do our best and finish it
on a good note, that's wrong?

00:12:47.700 --> 00:12:51.540
It seems Kaleido Stage is going to end
because it should end.

00:12:52.410 --> 00:12:53.770
I don't understand!

00:12:53.770 --> 00:12:57.140
What are you trying to say, Boss?

00:12:57.910 --> 00:12:59.780
I'm disappointed in you.

00:13:02.280 --> 00:13:06.780
What else can we do?

00:13:27.440 --> 00:13:29.910
I'm disappointed in you.

00:13:29.980 --> 00:13:31.480
I don't understand.

00:13:31.480 --> 00:13:33.000
What does he want me to do?

00:13:35.780 --> 00:13:36.720
Sora!

00:13:36.720 --> 00:13:37.850
Ken!

00:13:37.850 --> 00:13:39.550
What are you doing here?

00:13:39.550 --> 00:13:41.720
I've been looking for you.

00:13:41.720 --> 00:13:42.850
Sorry...

00:13:43.560 --> 00:13:44.760
What?

00:13:44.760 --> 00:13:46.230
I see...

00:13:46.230 --> 00:13:48.350
The Boss told you something like that.

00:13:48.500 --> 00:13:51.770
What shall I do? It's our last show.

00:13:51.770 --> 00:13:55.260
And I have to appear on stage halfhearted
like the way I feel now.

00:13:55.940 --> 00:13:58.140
No matter what Boss told you,

00:13:58.140 --> 00:14:01.940
everyone united because they want to do
their best since this will be the last show.

00:14:02.240 --> 00:14:03.340
I know.

00:14:03.410 --> 00:14:07.350
Unless you pull yourself together,
everyone will fall apart.

00:14:09.220 --> 00:14:11.010
Sorry, Ken.

00:14:11.250 --> 00:14:12.740
Please let me go back to the
dormitory for just a little while.

00:14:13.090 --> 00:14:15.020
Oh... Okay.

00:14:15.360 --> 00:14:17.060
Please don't be late for
the raising of the curtain.

00:14:17.060 --> 00:14:17.850
Yes.

00:14:24.570 --> 00:14:26.860
Fool! Fool?

00:14:28.940 --> 00:14:29.730
Fool?

00:14:30.070 --> 00:14:31.660
Hey, listen, Fool.

00:14:32.740 --> 00:14:34.770
Please don't hide. Please come out.

00:14:36.040 --> 00:14:39.170
Don't tell me I can't see him anymore...

00:14:39.710 --> 00:14:41.080
Fool! Where are you?!

00:14:41.620 --> 00:14:42.670
Hey, Fool!

00:14:43.280 --> 00:14:44.770
I have something I want you to listen to!

00:14:45.750 --> 00:14:47.050
Please show up.

00:14:47.660 --> 00:14:49.050
Please don't be mean.

00:14:49.760 --> 00:14:53.090
I don't understand what the Boss is saying!

00:14:53.230 --> 00:14:56.920
Fool! Please answer me!

00:14:57.870 --> 00:14:59.900
I can't believe this.

00:14:59.900 --> 00:15:03.300
I lost the ability to see Fool.

00:15:03.640 --> 00:15:05.970
Listen, if you can see me,

00:15:05.970 --> 00:15:08.270
it means that you were chosen for the stage.

00:15:08.910 --> 00:15:11.680
Once, there was a man who was
able to see me.

00:15:11.680 --> 00:15:16.010
The man I was talking about
gradually lost the ability to see me.

00:15:21.790 --> 00:15:24.420
I lost the ability to stay at Kaleido Stage.

00:15:24.630 --> 00:15:27.250
And I was told something like that
by the Boss.

00:15:27.730 --> 00:15:30.360
I'm not able to see Fool, either.

00:15:30.970 --> 00:15:33.590
Everything is gone all at once.

00:15:34.340 --> 00:15:37.900
I don't know what I should do at all.

00:15:40.310 --> 00:15:44.610
So much has happened since
the first day I came to Kaleido Stage.

00:15:45.380 --> 00:15:47.370
But even when someone got angry with me
or when I made a mistake,

00:15:47.920 --> 00:15:50.280
I never felt like this.

00:15:52.050 --> 00:15:53.380
I see...

00:15:53.820 --> 00:15:56.190
I'm not able to see Fool

00:15:56.190 --> 00:16:00.720
because I can never do the legendary
great maneuver the way I am now.

00:16:01.430 --> 00:16:06.300
It's not like I lost the feeling that
I want to be as good as Miss Layla.

00:16:06.300 --> 00:16:08.460
That hasn't changed even now, but...

00:16:11.940 --> 00:16:16.600
Today is the last day I can appear
on the same stage with Miss Layla.

00:16:18.180 --> 00:16:23.550
Mia, Anna and I have been encouraging
each other until today.

00:16:23.550 --> 00:16:27.320
I wanted to keep doing shows
together even after this,

00:16:29.890 --> 00:16:35.660
but our Kaleido Stage
will be gone starting tomorrow.

00:16:36.260 --> 00:16:37.770
Then,

00:16:37.770 --> 00:16:39.970
I thought in the end I should
perform my best for "Freedom"

00:16:39.970 --> 00:16:43.200
which we all created together.

00:16:43.200 --> 00:16:45.870
And yet the Boss told me, it would be
better if we just don't do it.

00:16:45.870 --> 00:16:47.930
What does he mean?

00:16:51.750 --> 00:16:53.610
Still, I have to go.

00:16:53.610 --> 00:16:57.740
No matter how I feel,
the curtain will still be raised.

00:16:59.550 --> 00:17:01.490
Okay! I'm going!

00:17:11.900 --> 00:17:15.300
But when I think that today
will be the last, l...

00:17:15.300 --> 00:17:16.360
Oh...

00:17:23.040 --> 00:17:24.410
Thank you.

00:17:24.480 --> 00:17:25.410
Miss Layla...

00:17:25.980 --> 00:17:28.280
It's likely we won't see each other again.

00:17:28.280 --> 00:17:29.780
Don't act so tough.

00:17:29.780 --> 00:17:32.280
I will talk to Mr. Hamilton.

00:17:32.790 --> 00:17:34.890
No matter how hard you guys try,

00:17:34.890 --> 00:17:37.360
your Kaleido Stage will be over after today.

00:17:37.630 --> 00:17:40.360
I'm not thinking that today is the last day.

00:17:40.360 --> 00:17:41.260
What?

00:17:41.800 --> 00:17:44.770
Hey, look at the reality, Layla.

00:17:44.770 --> 00:17:48.760
Yuri, did you see our show?

00:17:49.040 --> 00:17:50.730
"Our"?

00:17:50.910 --> 00:17:52.430
That's not the way you usually talk.

00:17:53.740 --> 00:17:57.970
Sorry, but I don't think it's worth seeing.

00:17:59.250 --> 00:18:00.410
"Freedom"...

00:18:01.080 --> 00:18:04.150
It's a story about young people
who believe in the future.

00:18:04.150 --> 00:18:05.490
In the story,

00:18:05.490 --> 00:18:08.820
you can see those lively young people
doing their best for tomorrow

00:18:08.820 --> 00:18:10.790
in spite of fighting each other.

00:18:12.390 --> 00:18:14.880
The character I'm playing is
also that kind of person.

00:18:15.230 --> 00:18:19.390
She really believes that she can
have the future that she is hoping for.

00:18:20.470 --> 00:18:22.260
The others are the same too.

00:18:22.640 --> 00:18:24.370
No matter what kind of tough
circumstances they face,

00:18:24.370 --> 00:18:26.900
they are never overcome with sorrow
while they do nothing.

00:18:27.610 --> 00:18:29.800
All the characters have that kind of strength.

00:18:30.080 --> 00:18:33.710
And I like the nature of that show.

00:18:35.550 --> 00:18:37.650
Even if Kaleido Stage closes its doors,

00:18:37.650 --> 00:18:40.380
it can't close the door to my future.

00:18:40.550 --> 00:18:45.760
It will not be my last show,
unless I wish it.

00:18:45.760 --> 00:18:47.530
That's what I believe.

00:18:47.530 --> 00:18:50.430
At least, if I couldn't believe that,

00:18:50.430 --> 00:18:52.370
I couldn't appear on this stage.

00:18:54.400 --> 00:18:56.530
That is such a hackneyed,
idealistic point of view.

00:18:57.470 --> 00:18:59.340
You think that way.

00:18:59.340 --> 00:19:01.740
Because you don't believe in your future.

00:19:09.850 --> 00:19:10.870
Miss Layla.

00:19:11.350 --> 00:19:12.340
Sora!

00:19:13.690 --> 00:19:16.050
Sorry, I heard your conversation.

00:19:17.290 --> 00:19:20.390
So, today is not the end of the show, is it?

00:19:22.060 --> 00:19:26.330
I don't want to make it the
end of the show as of today either.

00:19:27.000 --> 00:19:29.370
Even after this,

00:19:29.370 --> 00:19:31.610
I want to appear on the stage
many more times with you.

00:19:31.610 --> 00:19:33.210
Sora, hurry.

00:19:33.210 --> 00:19:36.340
The curtain will be raised as scheduled.

00:19:36.340 --> 00:19:37.830
Yes.

00:19:38.480 --> 00:19:40.650
We're not going to do our best
because it is the last.

00:19:40.650 --> 00:19:42.580
We will do our best today, tomorrow,
and the day after tomorrow.

00:19:43.180 --> 00:19:45.350
And we're going to put on
our best show all the time.

00:19:45.350 --> 00:19:46.390
Yes!

00:19:46.390 --> 00:19:49.520
It's not like the audience is
interested in seeing a sad show.

00:19:49.520 --> 00:19:50.320
It's true.

00:19:50.790 --> 00:19:53.960
This is what the Boss meant.

00:19:53.960 --> 00:19:54.830
Right. Right.

00:19:55.130 --> 00:19:57.100
It seems like you're finally
back to who you are.

00:19:58.370 --> 00:20:01.770
Anyhow, as I thought, Miss Layla is amazing.

00:20:01.770 --> 00:20:02.740
Yes, she is.

00:20:03.870 --> 00:20:06.860
Maybe, I don't want to lose...

00:20:07.440 --> 00:20:10.880
I don't want to lose the partner
who motivates me so much...

00:20:10.880 --> 00:20:14.040
If you start doing something new,
you will forget about it soon enough.

00:20:15.720 --> 00:20:18.050
There is no way I can forget...

00:20:18.590 --> 00:20:20.390
Just remembering Miss Layla's words,

00:20:20.390 --> 00:20:23.560
"It will not be my last show,
unless I wish it. "

00:20:23.560 --> 00:20:27.760
makes me so emotional I could cry.

00:20:27.960 --> 00:20:29.790
Oh, I messed up my makeup.

00:20:29.960 --> 00:20:31.590
Sorry, can you go before me?

00:20:35.500 --> 00:20:36.300
Miss Layla!

00:20:36.640 --> 00:20:37.470
Where is Sora?

00:20:37.740 --> 00:20:39.770
She messed up her makeup right now, and...

00:20:39.770 --> 00:20:41.240
She is fixing it.

00:20:46.350 --> 00:20:47.180
Sora...

00:20:47.180 --> 00:20:48.880
Oh, Miss Layla.

00:20:48.880 --> 00:20:52.150
Oh... I'm doing my best to hurry, but...

00:20:54.590 --> 00:20:55.920
Give it to me.

00:20:55.920 --> 00:20:56.720
What?

00:20:57.060 --> 00:20:58.920
I will do it for you.

00:20:59.190 --> 00:21:00.160
What?

00:21:05.270 --> 00:21:07.030
Oh... Miss Layla...

00:21:07.030 --> 00:21:09.940
Don't talk. I can't do my work.

00:21:09.940 --> 00:21:11.000
Oh...

00:21:16.540 --> 00:21:19.010
I enjoyed co-starring on stage with you.

00:21:21.780 --> 00:21:23.380
Miss Layla...

00:21:23.380 --> 00:21:25.390
Why would you say something like that?

00:21:25.390 --> 00:21:27.550
This is not the end, right?

00:21:28.190 --> 00:21:30.250
Right?

00:21:30.820 --> 00:21:32.260
Now, it looks good.

00:21:32.890 --> 00:21:34.260
Let's go, Sora.

00:21:34.460 --> 00:21:35.260
Yes.

00:21:46.910 --> 00:21:47.810
Fool...

00:21:48.280 --> 00:21:51.710
Can you see me again?

00:21:52.850 --> 00:21:54.710
Yes, unfortunately.

00:21:56.180 --> 00:21:57.320
The Sun.

00:21:57.320 --> 00:22:00.220
This card represents a hope for tomorrow.

00:22:00.420 --> 00:22:02.320
A hope for tomorrow.

00:22:03.220 --> 00:22:04.090
That's nice.

00:22:05.760 --> 00:22:06.560
That's right!

00:22:06.630 --> 00:22:10.590
Starting tomorrow,
our performance will start!

00:22:20.310 --> 00:22:22.280
Next Kaleido Star

00:22:23.080 --> 00:22:25.880
Don't say something ridiculous!
Of course, I'm worried.

00:22:25.950 --> 00:22:28.480
And so, after we were
kicked out of the dormitory,

00:22:28.480 --> 00:22:30.320
I'm going to stay at
Ken's house for a while.

00:22:30.320 --> 00:22:32.910
But, Sora's worried parents
came to see her, and...

00:22:32.990 --> 00:22:34.460
What's more, inside of her mother's body...

00:22:34.460 --> 00:22:35.920
There is a new life,

00:22:35.920 --> 00:22:38.330
my father and mother's real child.

00:22:38.330 --> 00:22:41.450
Where is the place I can go back to?
Where? Where?

00:22:41.860 --> 00:22:43.260
Next time on Kaleido Star,
"Amazing Family Ties"

00:22:43.260 --> 00:22:45.830
Amazing Family Ties

00:22:43.260 --> 00:22:45.830
Next time on Kaleido Star,
"Amazing Family Ties"

00:22:45.830 --> 00:22:47.840
Amazing Family Ties

00:22:45.830 --> 00:22:47.840
My wings are my dream
and on towards the sky...

00:22:47.840 --> 00:22:48.100
Amazing Family Ties

00:22:51.510 --> 00:23:04.220
<i>Boku wa koko ni iru
sora to michi no aida de mukai kaze</i>

00:22:51.510 --> 00:23:04.220
<i>I'm here between the sky and the roads,
and facing against the wind</i>

00:23:04.220 --> 00:23:18.030
<i>Soshite mae o muiteiru
Mou nido to kanashimi ga furanai youni to</i>

00:23:04.220 --> 00:23:18.030
<i>And I'm facing forward so the sorrow
doesn't rain down ever again</i>

00:23:18.030 --> 00:23:24.070
<i>Ano kabe o koete kokomade kitanda</i>

00:23:18.030 --> 00:23:24.070
<i>I came all the way here after
I jumped over that wall</i>

00:23:24.070 --> 00:23:31.350
<i>Nigedashitaku naru koto wa nando mo aru</i>

00:23:24.070 --> 00:23:31.350
<i>There are many times
when I just want to run away</i>

00:23:31.350 --> 00:23:36.680
<i>Dakedo kokoni irunara taishite bibitte inai</i>

00:23:31.350 --> 00:23:36.680
<i>But I'm still here,
so, I'm not daunted that much</i>

00:23:36.680 --> 00:23:44.120
<i>Kakinaguri no uta "hajimekara yareba iisa"</i>

00:23:36.680 --> 00:23:44.120
<i>The poem I scribbled down, I can just
start writing over from the beginning</i>

00:23:44.120 --> 00:23:49.790
<i>Umaku kakenaku te boku wa waratte iru</i>

00:23:44.120 --> 00:23:49.790
<i>Unable to write it well, I'm laughing</i>
